Z||000000||sluppy123||05-03-2000||10:45 PM||||I'm getting a new windshield put in one of my GT's and I've got a ??<P> The plastic strip that fills the gap between the glass and the body, will they put a new one in? Mine is cracked and broken Is this a special part that needs to be ordered?<P>TIA-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||05-03-2000||10:58 PM||||   That's the window moulding. They probably will for an additional fee. I'm not sure what they charge for a windshield replacement in your area, but I can get a windshield with new moulding for around $150.00. And that's done in my driveway.<P>  Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||Ozzy||05-03-2000||11:54 PM||||Damn BAM-BAM! Thats cheap! I get a pretty good discount from the local auto glass shop 'cause I give 'em all my windshield business for the company fleet on my project(65 trucks) and the lowest they have quoted me for the GT is $200!<P>Maybe I need to offer the business to SOMEONE else huh?<P>Ozzy||||reg||4
Z||000003||GT Bastard||05-04-2000||01:37 AM||||They usually give you a new one included in the price.  At least they did for me... It was only 120 bucks, and they did an awesome job.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sage||05-04-2000||12:08 PM||||Just put new one in my sons 88 for 125.00.  Comes with new molding on it, and they did it in my garage.  Triumph Glass.  Took about 10 min. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||05-04-2000||02:27 PM||||Make sure a reputable place that knows what they're doing replaces your Fiero windshield. They require a special adhesive that actually bonds the glass to the body. You don't want that baby popping out if you hit the brakes hard.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GT||05-04-2000||06:30 PM||||Thats strange, Triumph glass put a new windshield and molding on my car for $222!  I see someone said Triumph did theres for $125!  hhhmmm.. I called and got estimates for my windshield and found Triumph to be the cheapest and one other place wanted $420!!  I hung up. lol||||reg||1
Z||000007||pollock||05-05-2000||03:51 PM||||At the glass shop where i used to work, we called that stuff roll moulding, because we bought it in bulk on a roll.  It's the exact same for dozens of cars, including the Fiero.  <P>Batboy, you're right... you should definitely go to a reputable shop, but there's nothing special about a Fiero windshield.  It's glued in with a urethane sealer, just like practically all cars now.   ||||reg||14
Z||000008||Sage||05-05-2000||05:02 PM||||Triumph used the adhesive you refer to and applied it from a "squeeze tube"(looked like large caulking gun).  It appears to be the same stuff that was on there originally.  Had the front half of the roof off(color change paint job after a wreck) and used the stuff that comes in a roll to bond the top back on.  Seems to be the same or better than what the factory used.  It starts out round about 3/4" round, and then smashes down.||||reg||1
